is" 1182 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to zero due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(-x)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)({e}^{(-x)}+{e}^{-(-x)}) \\\\  & =-x({e}^{-x}+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-x)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) \\\\  & \\ne -h(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c1ec128486d1779cde54681fee1a120288070b2589fe0b7e6859e2636d19e74" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947