ture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the integral ${\\int }_{-\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x$ using symmetry." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2134f970e7a0b23a4a30b3e6f3f7b73952ba595d7d32f9ad090226fa8e65572" "basis" 1730 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡((-x)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2134f970e7a0b23a4a30b3e6f3f7b73952ba595d7d32f9ad090226fa8e65572" "basis" 1730 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c002ce762d4568a9d06022c78795386c23fbe7302eb25e745b08c2161835273c" "basis" 1730 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2134f970e7a0b23a4a30b3e6f3f7b73952ba595d7d32f9ad090226fa8e65572" "basis" 1730 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2134f970e7a0b23a4a30b3e6f3f7b73952ba595d7d32f9ad090226fa8e65572" "basis" 1730 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answe