730 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2134f970e7a0b23a4a30b3e6f3f7b73952ba595d7d32f9ad090226fa8e65572" "basis" 1730 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041046/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-88689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(-x)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) \\\\  & \\ne -f(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is an odd function, but integral II is not of the form ${\\int }_{-a}^{a}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ since the upper and lower limits are not opposites. Therefore, we cannot use symmetry to simplify the integral.\n\n- The function $h(x)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\  & =-h(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f8fc0877b95a6e04805946e97e9ff9bac9760ccd18322977ff35d8497af8be98"} {"question" "q-88689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to zero due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(-x)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)({e}^{(-x)}+{e}^{-(-x)}) \\\\  & =-x({e}^{-x}+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-x)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) \\\\  & \\ne -h(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f8fc0877b95a6e04805946e97e9ff9bac9760ccd18322977ff35d8497af8be98"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-88692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=A,$ what is the value of ${\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-x)^{3}) \\\\  & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-8}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+A & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =-A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f8fc0877b95a6e04805946e97e9ff9bac9760ccd18322977ff35d8497af8be98"} {"question" "q-156192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-A"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}A"] ["math" "2A"] ["math" "A"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-A"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the integral ${\\int }_{-\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x$ using symmetry." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡((-x)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f8fc0877b95a6e04805946e97e9ff9bac9760ccd18322977ff35d8497af8be98"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-156690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-316128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=p,$ express the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x$ in terms of $p.$\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-316128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x),$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x).$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x){e}^{(-x)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =-x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+p & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-316128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f8fc0877b95a6e04805946e97e9ff9bac9760ccd18322977ff35d8497af8be98"} {"question" "q-316128" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"} {"question" "q-316128" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-p"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069515/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbeaa087e11bff0038701f7e87a674b809100cbca7a75c0764c7cafe50a7fba"}] "usage" {"q-88692" [] "q-156690" [] "q-88689" []} "basis" 2386 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186291871 17592186291872 17592186291873 17592186291874 17592186291875 17592186293982 17592186293983 17592186293984 17592186293985 17592186293986 17592186328399 17592186328400 17592186328401 17592186328402 17592186328403] "immutable_fields" [[17592186291870 :answer-field/correct] [17592186291870 :answer-fiel